<div class="flex min-h-full flex-col justify-center px-6 py-12 lg:px-8">
  <div class="sm:mx-auto sm:w-full sm:max-w-sm">
    <h1 class="text-center text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900">Sign in to your account</h1>
    <%== render('_form_error') %>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-10 sm:mx-auto sm:w-full sm:max-w-sm">
    <form method="post" class="space-y-6 rodauth" role="form" id="login-form" autocomplete="on">
    <%== rodauth.csrf_tag %>
      <div>
        <label for="email" class="block text-sm font-medium leading-6 text-gray-900">Email address</label>
        <div class="mt-2">
          <%# The name is Rodauth's -- it reads the login out of a parameter called
              "login" and renaming it breaks the post -- but the id and the autofill token
              are ours. The token is "email", which is what this field asks for and the only
              thing an account is ever identified by here: there is no separate username to
              key a credential to, so naming one is describing a form this app does not have.
              "username" was tried and reverted; it is the more common recommendation for a
              sign-in identifier, and if a password manager is ever found not to offer a
              saved credential back here, that is the first thing to try again. It has to
              match the token on the sign-up form either way, which is asserted rather than
              left to whoever edits one of the two files. %>
          <input id="email" name="login" type="email" autocomplete="email" required
                        class="<%= field_style %> block w-full px-3 py-1.5 text-gray-900 placeholder:text-gray-400 sm:text-sm sm:leading-6">
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <%# A "Forgot password?" sat beside this label at href="#" for as long as the page
            existed. reset_password is not in the enable list in app.rb and this app
            configures no mailer, so there has never been anything behind it: it promised a
            way back in at the one moment somebody needs one, and then declined. Nothing
            replaces it, not even a line saying recovery does not exist, because that
            sentence would sit under every sign-in forever to deliver a verdict rather than
            a remedy. The link belongs here again once reset_password is enabled and a mail
            provider is wired up, and not before. %>
        <label for="password" class="block text-sm font-medium leading-6 text-gray-900">Password</label>
        <div class="mt-2">
          <input id="password" name="password" type="password" autocomplete="current-password" required
                        class="<%= field_style %> block w-full px-3 py-1.5 text-gray-900 placeholder:text-gray-400 sm:text-sm sm:leading-6">
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <button type="submit" class="<%= button_style %> flex w-full justify-center bg-lime-500 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-semibold leading-6 text-gray-900 hover:bg-lime-600">Sign in</button>
      </div>
    </form>

    <p class="mt-10 text-center text-sm text-gray-500">
      Need an account?
      <a href="/create-account" class="font-semibold leading-6 text-lime-700 hover:text-lime-800">Create an account</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
